# Unit tests (`%testharness`)

A **library** page: Schema + Methods, no Construction. The Target is the
test suite. Each `%with` embeds a WCHNT construction as a fixture; `%assert`
checks host expressions against that fixture. Re-`%with` the same class
rebinds the same name (`rect` below).

Run with `lein run examples/unittests.wcn`, then compile the emitted Haxe
(`haxe -main Main -neko unittests.n && neko unittests.n`).

Live twin: `live-examples/unittests.wcn` (`%testharness-live`).

## Schema

```
Rect = Int/w Int/h
Point = Int/x Int/y
```

## Methods

```
Rect::area = { w * h }

Rect::contains = { Point/p |
  (p.x >= 0) and (p.x < w) and (p.y >= 0) and (p.y < h)
}

Point::moved = { Int/dx, Int/dy | [:Point (x + dx) (y + dy)] }
```

## Target

```
%testharness

%with
[:Rect 10 20]

%assert
"area of 10x20"
rect.area() == 200

"origin is inside"
rect.contains(new Point(0, 0)) == true

"far corner is outside"
rect.contains(new Point(10, 20)) == false

%with
[:Rect 3 4]

%assert
"area of 3x4, failing assertion"
rect.area() == 11
"area of 3x4, succeeding assertion"
rect.area() == 12

%with
[:Point 5 7]

%assert
"moved right"
point.moved(3, 0).x == 8

"moved up"
point.moved(0, -2).y == 5
```
